{"id": "EUVD-2026-93099", "enisaUuid": "59fe7303-4af7-32d4-9323-df7f36fb2027", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix next_buffer UAF and NextCommand bounds in compound PDUs\n\nFix several related bounds checking and pointer lifecycle issues in\nreceive_encrypted_standard()'s handling of compound encrypted frames:\n\n- Clear next_buffer after assigning it to server->bigbuf. A stale\n  next_buffer pointer can lead to a use-after-free on subsequent\n  error paths.\n- Update pdu_length to the decrypted plaintext size (buf_size). Using\n  the pre-decryption length allows NextCommand to point into stale\n  ciphertext residue.\n- Reject next_cmd values smaller than MID_HEADER_SIZE(server).\n- Fix an integer overflow in the upper bound check by verifying\n  pdu_length - next_cmd < MID_HEADER_SIZE(server), ensuring the\n  trailing slice is large enough for a header.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:02", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72eaef1f37a3b6bec11c342736834dc3707be3e4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/491e33144dee872cffda207f6fcb09260728f803", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8749946579708ea0d339034bb7f423a67dbe89cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96c436e4b010711452b2872558938f4ef276492a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/858d5ac22cb889266993e7670f9f0c4f4aeedd78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05762c5bc1cfdcac36747994fde2c04387a457f1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-68gh-wq6f-89rf", "CVE-2026-98171"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a89584a-f242-3a9f-92da-4e054aeb597c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <858d5ac22cb889266993e7670f9f0c4f4aeedd78"}, {"id": "34e781d2-99c3-3aa4-af9a-5075d717ded5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <05762c5bc1cfdcac36747994fde2c04387a457f1"}, {"id": "4029cc0a-f7f1-3fa3-bfcc-f0e51583c4dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "4d05c216-4960-3f79-b666-281a3b1046b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <72eaef1f37a3b6bec11c342736834dc3707be3e4"}, {"id": "4e0d94f5-3bd7-37af-adbd-69dc69ca5b7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "91584fbb-56d1-3ceb-b8c7-5af02235dd52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "b96d82ed-ccf0-3768-8cb3-d5bc3d76fb4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b97dbe47-f0e6-3be4-ae86-8f5a4567a4c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "bf8a94d2-1ee0-3369-8d43-77d14acc2bf8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e04b1bdf-2372-376c-8ee0-ba74acdab5ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <491e33144dee872cffda207f6fcb09260728f803"}, {"id": "eeb5ca01-cb15-326c-a227-db5f6b7ab89c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <8749946579708ea0d339034bb7f423a67dbe89cf"}, {"id": "f1ca6b98-9cb9-3036-887e-9c07ec83c609", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "f359530d-5504-3f6d-912e-9474145a1c1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <96c436e4b010711452b2872558938f4ef276492a"}, {"id": "f7282a14-b9a1-3